    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0144" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg46"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5287: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-05-31T11:00:00+08:00">May 31, 1932—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 31—5:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>273. 1. Japanese Army completed evacuation area number 2 Kiangwan and Chinese
                    resumed complete control of this entire area May 29th.</p>
                <p>2. Last units of Japanese Army troops embark for Japan today May 31st.</p>
                <p>3. Japanese naval landing party take over and occupy barracks west of railroad
                    area number 1 Woosung with 100 gendarmes; area <pb facs="0145" n="47"
                        xml:id="pg47"/> number 3 Yinghsiang with 200 gendarmes and continue to hold
                    area number 4 Chapei with 2,000 marines.</p>
                <p>4. Chinese reoccupy Lunghwa with 200 gendarmes of 6th Regiment. Repeat to War
                    Department. Repeated to the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
